# Globus Maker

Web app to download an OSM region and generate globe meridian stripes (Panotools `slize.pl` pipeline).

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `FE/` | SvelteKit 5 static SPA + Leaflet/MapLibre |
| `BE/src/` | Hono API (shared by Worker and local dev server) |
| `worker.ts` | Cloudflare Worker entry — routes `/api/*` to Hono, else static assets |
| `container/` | Python/FastAPI processor (tile fetch, stitch, `slize.pl`, zip) |
| `shared/` | Cross-stack code (`map-style.ts`) imported via `@shared` alias |

## Local dev

`npm run dev` — starts processor (Docker `:8080`), API (`:8787`), and FE (`:5173`).

Individual services: `dev:processor`, `dev:api`, `dev:fe`. Skip processor: `npm run dev -- --no-processor`.

## Production

- Worker serves `FE/build` via `ASSETS` binding
- Jobs/artifacts in R2 bucket `globus-maker-artifacts`
- Processor via `GlobusProcessor` Container DO binding (leave `PROCESSOR_URL` empty)

## Conventions

- Keep `BE/src/types.ts` and `FE/src/lib/types.ts` in sync for API contracts
- Map layer types/logic live in `shared/map-style.ts` — don't duplicate
- Tile math lives in `BE/src/osm/tile-math.ts`; run `npm test` after changes
- Stripe height: `diameterCm × 160` px; width formula in `stripeWidthPx()`
- Job outputs are distorted **SVG** (zip + previews); globe preview may use a JPEG DePolar raster
- Job statuses: `queued` → `fetching_tiles` → `stitching` → `projecting` → `packaging` → `complete` | `failed`
